  "lineage": "Brazilian MPB (Música Popular Brasileira) post-bossa-nova-and-tropicália sophisticated-popular-music umbrella-tradition emerging 1965-onward from the bossa-nova-tropicália-festival circuit. Built on harmonically-extended chord-vocabulary (minor-7-and-maj-7-and-9-and-11 jazz-extensions), Brazilian-rhythmic foundation (samba, baião, choro, bossa derivatives), and singer-songwriter literary-poetic-lyrical-sophistication. The 1970s mpb-jovem-guarda commercial-pop wave, the 1980s mpb-de-câmara chamber-mpb, and 1990s-onward mpb-as-heritage-institution comprise the genre's historical arc. Canonical instrumentation: violão acoustic-guitar nylon-string fingerstyle-led, with optional flute, piano, cavaquinho, and contemporary-rhythm-section. The MPB-canon overlaps significantly with samba-canção and bossa-nova but retains a distinct singer-songwriter-as-poet aesthetic identity.",
